From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: leave display settings to the seat, send
 mode_requested

A SplitPlay worker runs in a desk's RDP loopback session. That session's
display (RdpIdd) is resized by the seat through the RDP display-control
channel; the worker must never change display settings, and above all
never touch the console's displays.

- display_device: on Windows no libdisplaydevice settings manager is
  created. Every display_device call becomes a pass-through: nothing is
  applied, reverted or "recovered" at start-up, map_output_name() returns
  the configured name unchanged, and allow_encoder_probing() no longer
  depends on libdisplaydevice's CCD view of the session.
- configure_display() (Moonlight /launch and /resume with no other
  stream running) sends the control event
  {"type":"event","name":"mode_requested","data":{"width":W,"height":H,"fps":F}}
  instead. If the desktop has another size, it then waits up to 3 s for
  the size to change, so that encoder probing and capture start on the
  new mode; any change ends the wait because the seat may round the size.
  Standalone (no --pipe) the mode is left as it is.
- dd_configuration_option is ignored, with a warning when it is set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J21Rm42dakZVfEnnyh7aQn

